  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">District and Community Health Services Revitalization Operation through the World Bank</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The District and Community Health Services Revitalization Program is to improve the utilization and quality of health care and nutrition services at district and community level with a focus on vulnerable populations. The Payment for Results supports interventions in 4 areas: (1) Promoting resilience, digitalization, and efficiency of the health system; (2) Improving health outcomes for mothers and adolescent girls; (3) Improving child health and nutrition; and (4) Prevention and care for communicable and non-communicable diseases. The program will finance capacity building to support the operation and supports restoration of health services and emergency preparedness and response in conflict-affected districts led by the Bank.</narrative>
  </description>
